cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EDNiX, please cite it using the metadata from this file (and the article once published)."
title: "EDNiX: a multi-species pipeline for anatomical, functional MRI and PET neuroimaging"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Garin
    given-names: Clément
    affiliation: "Institut des Sciences Cognitives Marc Jeannerod, CNRS UMR 5229, Lyon, France"
repository-code: "https://github.com/garincle/EDNiX"
url: "https://garincle.github.io/EDNiX/guide/"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  EDNiX takes BIDS datasets of rodents, bats, dogs, non-human primates and humans through anatomical,
  functional MRI and PET/CT preprocessing, brings every subject into a common cross-species atlas
  framework (multi-level EDNiX atlases, volume and cortical surface), and runs group and comparative
  analyses.
keywords:
  - neuroimaging
  - comparative neuroscience
  - MRI
  - fMRI
  - PET
  - BIDS
  - cross-species atlas
